UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 2022 in Bangor, Maine, Suncovia was established by solar industry professionals to create a more transparent and accessible path to solar energy for homeowners facing rising utility costs. The company operates with a fully in-house model, handling sales, installation, and service internally rather than outsourcing to third-party contractors.

Suncovia provides residential and commercial solar installation, roofing services, battery storage, and heat pump solutions. Its in-house teams manage the entire project lifecycle—from site assessment and permitting to installation, inspection, and utility interconnection. The company states that most solar installations are completed in a single day outside of winter conditions, and it offers an online monitoring app for energy production and usage.

Customers range from individual homeowners replacing unpredictable utility bills with fixed monthly payments to commercial clients aiming for long-term energy cost predictability.

Suncovia differentiates itself through a no-money-down financing option with fixed monthly payments, a fully in-house workforce that eliminates subcontractor handoffs, and a focus on proactive communication throughout the permitting and installation process. The firm was built to simplify the solar experience by combining transparent pricing, rapid installation timelines, and a single point of accountability from consultation through activation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Roofing services", "Battery storage installation", "Heat pump installation", "Energy monitoring app"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Renewable energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Installation typically completed in one day (excluding winter conditions)", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fully in-house team for sales, installation, and service", "No-money-down solar financing with fixed monthly payments", "Installation typically completed in one day (outside winter)", "All permits and inspections handled internally", "Online monitoring app for energy production and usage"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2022 -> /about", "Headquarters in Bangor, Maine -> db", "Fully in-house team for sales, installation, service -> /about, /services, /", "No-money-down financing with fixed monthly payments -> /, /about", "Services: residential solar, commercial solar, roofing, battery storage, heat pumps -> /services, /", "Serves homeowners in 12 states (CA, CT, FL, IL, ME, MD, MA, NH, PA, RI, TX) -> /, /about, /services", "Installation typically completed in one day outside winter -> /, /about", "Online monitoring app for energy production and usage -> / (products)", "Handles all permits and inspections internally -> /, /about", "Award-winning Top Solar Contractor (per blog) -> /about (blog snippet)"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Our team provide residential and commercial solar solutions backed by transparent communication, fast installation timelines, and a fully in-house team.", "founded_year": "2022", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='suncovia' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sundance Custom Steel is based in Sundance, Wyoming, with a second location in Piedmont, South Dakota. The company was founded in 2015 by Jay Pixley as a faith‑based, family‑owned operation with a vision to supply superior steel products and unmatched customer service to the Black Hills region.

The company manufactures steel roofing, siding, trim, and accessories, offering profiles such as TUFFRIB, RUGGED, PBR panel, snap‑lock, mechanical‑lock, and board‑and‑batten systems. After expanding to a larger facility in 2022, Sundance Custom Steel provides custom fabrication, precision manufacturing, and rigorous quality control, and also offers professional installation and project management for residential and commercial projects. A 48‑hour turnaround on approved orders is standard.

Customers include contractors and homeowners across Wyoming, South Dakota, Montana, and Nebraska. The product line serves both new construction and renovation in the residential and commercial building sectors.

