UPDATE companies SET description='SunPol Solar is an independent residential solar installer founded in 2024 and headquartered in Newington, Connecticut. The company was started on the premise that lowering a family''s energy costs returns both money and time to the household, allowing them to focus on priorities beyond the monthly electric bill. No founders are named in public materials.

SunPol designs, permits, and installs rooftop solar arrays and Tesla Powerwall 3 battery storage for homeowners across all 169 Connecticut towns and throughout Massachusetts. The company offers three financing paths: a flagship Prepaid Solar Program that bundles equipment, installation, monitoring, and maintenance into a single upfront payment with zero monthly charges for 25 years; a power purchase agreement with a fixed per-kWh rate and no upfront cost; and a traditional cash purchase.

The customer base is exclusively residential, with recent projects documented in Newington, Bristol, Farmington, Wolcott, Newtown, and Southington. Battery backup is frequently sized for critical loads such as refrigeration, lighting, Wi-Fi, and medical equipment including CPAP machines, oxygen concentrators, and insulin pumps.

SunPol differentiates itself by retaining ownership of prepaid-lease systems for the full 25-year term, providing a single point of accountability for service and repairs. The prepaid pricing is marketed at roughly 30 percent below a comparable cash purchase, and the company emphasizes local presence—permits, inspections, and interconnection are handled in-house by a Connecticut-based team.', certifications=ARRAY['Connecticut Home Improvement Contractor License HIC-0698394','Massachusetts Home Improvement Contractor License HIC-220128','BBB Accredited','CT Green Bank Approved','Fully Insured']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar PV system design and engineering", "Rooftop solar panel installation", "Tesla Powerwall 3 battery storage installation", "Permitting and utility interconnection management", "25-year system monitoring and maintenance (prepaid lease)", "Prepaid solar lease program administration", "Power Purchase Agreement (PPA) administration", "Cash purchase solar installation"], "industries": ["Residential solar installation", "Residential energy storage", "Home energy services"], "materials": ["Tier 1 solar panels", "Microinverters", "Lithium-ion battery cells (Tesla Powerwall 3)"], "equipment": ["Tesla Powerwall 3", "Tier 1 solar panels", "Microinverters"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single upfront payment covers 25 years of solar, monitoring, and maintenance with $0 monthly payments", "Company owns, operates, and maintains the system for the full 25-year lease term", "Prepaid lease pricing approximately 30% below cash purchase cost", "Premium Tier 1 solar panels and microinverters with 25-year warranties", "Local Connecticut team handles all permitting, inspection, and utility interconnection"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2024 -> /about", "Headquartered in Newington, Connecticut -> /about", "CT HIC #0698394 -> /about", "MA HIC #220128 -> /about", "BBB Accredited -> /about", "CT Green Bank Approved -> /about", "Fully Insured -> /about", "100+ installations completed -> /about", "5-star Google reviews (40+) -> /about", "Serves all 169 Connecticut towns and Massachusetts -> /about", "Offers Prepaid Solar Program, PPA, and cash purchase -> /", "Installs Tesla Powerwall 3 battery storage -> /", "Uses Premium Tier 1 panels and microinverters with 25-year warranties -> /about", "Address: 125B Rockwell Rd, Newington, CT 06111 -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "SunPol Solar is an independent residential solar company based in Newington, Connecticut, serving homeowners across Connecticut and Massachusetts.", "founded_year": "2024", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sunpol-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sunrise Electronics, Inc. operates from Elk Grove Village, Illinois, where it was founded in 1997 as a family-owned business. The company began with a focus on building lasting customer relationships through reliable printed circuit board manufacturing.

The company fabricates a full spectrum of PCBs under one roof, from single-sided prototypes to 50-layer multilayer, HDI, rigid-flex, and flex circuits. Its facility handles panel sizes up to 24 by 30 inches, supports copper weights from 0.5 to 10 ounces, and offers surface finishes including ENIG, HASL, immersion silver, and hard gold. Production spans quick-turn prototypes — with same-day and 12-hour options — through high-volume runs managed with strategic supply-chain oversight.

Aerospace and defense programs represent core markets, supported by ITAR-aware processes and full traceability. The shop also serves medical and military applications, manufacturing to IPC-A-600 Class 2 and Class 3 standards.

Sunrise emphasizes in-house control from bare laminate to finished board, citing internal yields and low defect rates. The operation holds ±5% impedance as standard (±3% on request), achieves 3 mil trace and space, and maintains a 15:1 drill aspect ratio, positioning itself on speed and precision without outsourcing.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR','RoHS','ISO 9000','IPC-A-600 Class 2','IPC-A-600 Class 3','UL']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Quick-turn prototype fabrication (12-hour, 24h, 48h, 5-day)", "High-volume production with supply-chain management", "Multilayer PCB fabrication (2\u201350 layers)", "HDI / microvia technology (laser drilling, stacked, staggered, stacked-on-buried, variable-depth)", "Rigid-flex and flex circuit fabrication", "Blind and buried vias, via-in-pad with conductive/non-conductive fill", "Controlled impedance (\u00b15% standard, \u00b13% on request)", "Fine line and spacing (down to 1 mil/1 mil)", "Advanced via structures: back-drilling, counter bores, Cu-filled through holes, VIPPO", "Embedded passives (buried capacitance, buried resistors)", "Cavity construction", "Mixed-dielectric (hybrid) stackups", "Copper core construction", "Edge plating and castellated holes", "Surface finishes: ENIG, ENEPIG, hard gold, HASL, LF-HASL, OSP, immersion Ag/Sn", "Solder mask: LPI/LDI/UV (multiple colors)", "Impedance, flying probe, and HiPot testing", "In-house manufacturing under one roof", "Panel sizes up to 24\" x 30\"", "Drill aspect ratio up to 15:1", "Mechanical drilling down to 6 mil, laser drilling down to 3 mil", "Copper weight 0.5\u201310 oz", "IPC-A-600 Class 2 and Class 3 compliance", "ITAR-aware processing"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Medical", "Military"], "materials": ["Polyimide", "Rigid-flex", "Copper core"], "equipment": ["Pico/CO2 laser drilling equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same day, 24h, 48h, 5-day standard for prototypes", "tolerances": "\u00b15% impedance (standard), \u00b13% on request; 3 mil trace/space; 6 mil mechanical / 3 mil laser drilled holes; 15:1 drill aspect ratio", "built_on": ["Prototype completion in 12 hours (same-day available)", "In-house manufacturing from bare laminate to finished board", "ITAR-aware and ISO 9000 quality system with IPC Class 2/3 certification", "Family-owned with over two decades supporting mission-critical aerospace and defense programs", "Industry-leading internal yields and lowest defect rates"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1997 -> db", "Headquarters Elk Grove Village, Illinois -> db and homepage", "Family-owned -> FAQ page", "ITAR registered and ITAR-aware -> db, homepage, FAQ, capabilities", "ISO 9000 quality standards -> FAQ", "IPC-A-600 Class 2 and Class 3 -> FAQ, capabilities", "UL certification -> capabilities", "RoHS compliance -> db, capabilities", "12-hour prototype lead time -> homepage, capabilities", "Same-day, 24h, 48h, 5-day standard lead times -> capabilities", "In-house manufacturing start to finish -> FAQ", "2-50 layer multilayer capability -> homepage, capabilities", "Maximum panel size 24x30 inches -> homepage, capabilities", "Drill aspect ratio 15:1 -> homepage, capabilities", "3 mil trace/space, 6 mil mechanical/3 mil laser holes -> FAQ", "Controlled impedance \u00b15% standard, \u00b13% on request -> FAQ", "Surface finishes: ENIG, HASL, LF-HASL, OSP, Immersion Ag/Sn, Hard Gold -> capabilities", "Solder mask colors: Green, Black, Red, Blue, White, Yellow, Matte -> capabilities", "Rigid-flex, flex, HDI, embedded passives, cavity, copper core -> capabilities", "Advanced microvias: Pico/CO2 laser drilling -> capabilities", "Aerospace and defense core markets -> FAQ", "Medical and military applications -> FAQ, capabilities", "Industry-leading internal yields and lowest defect rates -> homepage", "Copper weight 0.5-10 oz -> capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "From single-sided prototypes through 50-layer rigid-flex and HDI builds, every Sunrise PCB is fabricated in our Elk Grove Village, IL facility \u2014 start to finish, under one roof.", "founded_year": "1997", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered", "ITAR-aware"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sunrise-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Superior Machine & Welding operates from a 10,000-square-foot facility on Ship Avenue in Anchorage, Alaska. The shop traces its roots to 1950 when Jack L. Whitmore purchased the original 3,400-square-foot operation and later reclaimed land from Ship Creek to expand. A 1964 addition brought the current footprint and added two Lodge & Shipley oil-country lathes and a five-ton overhead crane. Today the business is owned by Jantina Lunsford, a WOSB-certified woman owner and daughter of the previous proprietor, continuing the family-owned legacy.

The shop provides full-service machining, welding, and custom fabrication. Machining capacity includes two large-bore lathes with 28-inch swing and 40-foot material capacity, a five-axis and a three-axis horizontal boring mill, three Bridgeport-style knee mills with rotary tables, a two-axis CNC toolroom lathe, a custom-controlled CNC knee mill, a 4×8 CNC plasma/oxy-fuel cutter, an 18-inch Blanchard grinder holding ±0.00038 inch, a 24-inch vertical shaper for internal keyways, and 40- and 160-ton hydraulic presses for straightening. Welding covers TIG, MIG, stick, and brazing on materials from mild steel and aluminum to exotic alloys such as Inconel, Hastelloy, and titanium; the shop is noted for cast-iron repair and aluminum TIG work.

Customers span nearly every sector in Alaska: marine, heavy equipment, oilfield, trailers, wood-stove manufacturers, federal and military agencies, state and local government, corporations, and private citizens. The company emphasizes that local presence offsets higher pricing versus Lower-48 shops by eliminating shipping delays and providing rapid turnaround.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Manual and CNC machining", "Large-bore turning (up to 28\" swing, 40 ft length)", "Horizontal boring (5-axis and 3-axis)", "Vertical knee milling (Bridgeport-style with rotary tables)", "CNC toolroom lathe (2-axis)", "Custom CNC knee mill (in-house controller)", "CNC plasma/oxy-fuel cutting (4x8 ft, up to 1\" mild steel)", "Blanchard grinding (\u00b10.00038\")", "Tool post / centerless grinding", "Vertical shaping (internal keyways, splines up to 4 ft dia.)", "Hydraulic pressing (40 and 160 ton)", "Horizontal and vertical band sawing", "Thread chasing (API, NPT, ACME, buttress, metric, custom)", "Gear cutting (spur gears, OD splines)", "TIG welding (steel, stainless, aluminum, exotic alloys)", "MIG / wire-feed welding", "Stick welding", "Brazing (up to 100,000 PSI rods, 1200\u00b0F)", "Cast iron repair welding", "Shaft/bore buildup for re-machining", "Custom fabrication", "Precision line boring"], "industries": ["Marine", "Heavy equipment", "Oil and gas", "Government / military", "State and local government", "Construction / trailers", "Wood heating (wood stoves)", "General industrial repair"], "materials": ["Mild steel", "Alloy steel", "T1 steel", "Chromoly", "Stainless steel (all grades including 17-4PH)", "Cast iron", "Cast steel", "Aluminum", "Silicon bronze", "Inconel", "Stellite", "Hastelloy", "Turbaloy", "High-speed steel (HSS)", "Titanium", "Copper", "Brass alloys (brazing)"], "equipment": ["Lodge & Shipley Oil Country big bore lathes (2)", "5-axis horizontal boring mill (manual, 38\" XYZ travel, 3000 lb table)", "3-axis horizontal boring mill (larger table)", "Bridgeport-style vertical knee mills with rotary tables (3)", "2-axis CNC toolroom lathe", "CNC-adapted Bridgeport mill (custom in-house controller and motor)", "4x8 CNC plasma cutter with oxy-fuel capability", "40-ton hydraulic press", "160-ton hydraulic press", "18-inch HE&M horizontal band saw (48\" feed, \u00b10.010\" repeatability)", "14-inch vertical band saw", "18-inch Blanchard grinder (\u00b10.00038\" thickness tolerance)", "Dumore precision tool post grinder", "24-inch vertical shaper (12\" stroke, 4\" taper)", "Lincoln TIG welders (2)", "Miller stick welders (2)", "Miller CPU-controlled power supply with steel/aluminum wire feeders"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1950 by Jack L. Whitmore -> /about", "Current owner Jantina Lunsford, WOSB certified -> /about", "Facility 10,000 sq ft, expanded 1964 -> /about", "Location 1745 Ship Ave, Anchorage, AK -> /", "Machining equipment list -> /services", "Welding capabilities and materials -> /services", "Industries served: marine, heavy equipment, oilfield, government, private -> /about, /", "Quality guarantee: rework defects free -> /quality", "Local advantage vs Lower 48 shipping -> /about", "Cast iron repair expertise -> /services", "Custom CNC controller built in-house -> /services", "Blanchard grinder tolerance \u00b10.00038\" -> /services", "CNC lathe repeatability within tenths -> /services", "Band saw repeatability \u00b10.010\" -> /services"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Full service means we can do nearly anything in the field of machine repair.", "founded_year": "1950", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='superior-machine-welding-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SurePoint Electronics operates from Atwood, Kansas, a high-plains town in Rawlins County. The company was founded as a subsidiary of SurePoint Ag, a manufacturer of precision agriculture systems, with the goal of supplying high-quality electronics to the precision agriculture market. Ownership remains with the parent company, and no individual founders are named in public materials.

The shop produces OEM-quality wire harnesses, cable assemblies, and complete electronics assemblies including box builds, circuit boards, and controllers. Manufacturing combines automated equipment with hand assembly, and every harness undergoes Cirrus computer-interfaced testing for pin-out, continuity, resistance, and functionality. The team also provides harness braiding for agricultural, automotive, and heavy-equipment applications, and offers full-service development from concept through prototype to production with on-staff engineering support.

While its primary customer is its parent company, SurePoint Ag Systems, the business serves external OEMs in precision agriculture, general agriculture, automotive, and heavy equipment. It targets companies that need reliable wire harnessing, cable assemblies, and electronics manufacturing.

