UPDATE companies SET description='Technical & Assembly Services Corporation (TASC) was founded in 1991 by Richard Hirst, a U.S. Air Force veteran, in Seattle, Washington. The veteran-owned company grew from Hirst’s career spanning every phase of electronics manufacturing, from consumer innovations such as electronic chess games and automated apple-labeling machines to mission-critical systems like the emergency oxygen mask lighting for the Boeing 777.

TASC provides full-service electronics manufacturing and assembly, including printed circuit board assembly, cable and wire harness assembly, full electronic equipment box builds, prototypes, design and development, testing, troubleshooting, repair, rework, transformer/toroid/coil winding, and potting and conformal coating. The shop runs flexible production lines capable of high-volume, low-volume, and single-unit runs from its Seattle facility, serving clients nationwide.

The company supports OEMs, Fortune 500 firms, aerospace, medical equipment, U.S. military, government agencies and contractors, universities, entrepreneurs, inventors, and designers. Past projects include components for the U.S. Navy, Department of Defense, Homeland Security applications, and a specialized computer-interconnect device used on the M1A1 Abrams tank, as well as work for Bally gaming machines, espresso machines, and body-fat analyzers.

TASC emphasizes domestic manufacturing, ITAR registration, ISO 9001 compliance, and IPC Class II/III workmanship standards. Its differentiators include expedited assembly services, consignment and turnkey programs, materials management with obsolete-part workarounds, and a quality system built around first-article and in-process inspections.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','IPC-A-610/620 Class II','IPC-A-610/620 Class III','RoHS','ITAR','UL certifiable']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board (PCB) Assembly", "Cable & Wire Harness Assembly", "Full Electronic Equipment Box Builds", "Prototypes and Demo Units", "Design and Development", "Testing", "Troubleshooting, Repair, Rework", "Transformer, Toroid, and Coil Winding", "Potting and Conformal Coating", "Materials Management and Parts Sourcing", "Obsolete Parts Workarounds", "Reverse Engineering for Legacy Equipment", "Working with Incomplete Documentation"], "industries": ["OEMs", "Fortune 500", "Aerospace", "Medical Equipment", "U.S. Military", "Government Agencies and Contractors", "Universities", "Entrepreneurs", "Inventors", "Designers"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "High-volume, low-volume, and 1-up runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Expedited assembly services with quick-turn, consignment, and turnkey options", "ITAR registered and compliant with IPC-A-610/620 Class II and III", "Veteran-owned with deep defense and aerospace manufacturing experience", "Full-service from design through box build, testing, and repair", "Domestic production with materials management and obsolete-part workarounds"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1991 by Richard Hirst (US Air Force veteran) -> /about", "Veteran-owned -> /about", "Headquarters Seattle, Washington -> /about", "Services: PCB assembly, cable/harness, box builds, prototypes, design, testing, repair, winding, potting -> /services", "Certifications: ISO 9001, IPC Class II/III, RoHS, ITAR, UL certifiable -> /quality", "Industries served: OEMs, Fortune 500, aerospace, medical, military, government, universities, entrepreneurs -> /", "Projects: Boeing 777 oxygen mask lighting, Bally gaming, espresso machines, body-fat analyzers, Homeland Security, US Navy, DoD, M1A1 Abrams tank interconnect -> /about", "Expedited assembly, consignment, turnkey, quick turn -> /", "Materials management, obsolete parts workarounds -> /", "Domestic manufacturing (Made in USA) -> /", "Quality standards: first article inspections, in-process inspections, process controls, ESD protection, IP protection, NIST security -> /quality", "Management team names -> /about", "Flexible production lines for any size job -> /", "Reverse engineering, incomplete documentation -> /", "Proprietary techniques and quality control methodologies -> /", "Assembly Process Specification custom document -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "High-Quality Electronics Manufacturing and Assembly", "founded_year": "1991", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR Registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tasc-technical-assembly-services-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='TCS Electronics, Inc. was founded in 2012 in Farmington, New York. The company operates as a contract electronics manufacturer, providing PCB assemblies, cable and wire harnesses, and full electro-mechanical box builds.

The firm’s capabilities span printed circuit board assembly — including surface-mount, through-hole, multilayer, and flexible circuits — custom cable and wire harness assembly using wire gauges from 30 to 4/0, and electromechanical box-build integration performed with its sister company, TCS Industries, Inc. Testing services cover flying-probe inspection (outsourced) and functional test programs built on National Instruments LabView. Additional offerings include conformal coating, high-speed machining, cutting, component engineering for obsolescence management, and fulfillment services. The company describes its range as “prototyping to full production.”

TCS serves military, commercial and industrial, transportation, medical, and telecommunications customers. Its client base includes several major tier-one military suppliers and other electronics and technology companies operating nationally and globally.

The company emphasizes its management of a global supply chain, adherence to AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015 quality systems, and IPC-610/620 Class II workmanship (with Class III available) as factors that allow customers to outsource non-core manufacturing and focus on product development.', certifications=ARRAY['SAE AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015','ITAR','UL E157252','CSA LR109165-1','IPC-610','IPC-620','IPC-J-STD','Certified Tyco/AMP subcontractor']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB assembly (surface mount, through-hole, multilayer, flexible)", "Cable and wire harness assembly (30\u20134/0 AWG, coaxial, solid, stranded, metallic, sheathed, ribbon)", "Electromechanical box build assembly", "Flying probe testing (off-site)", "Functional testing (LabView-based)", "Conformal coating", "High-speed machining", "Cutting", "Component engineering (obsolescence management)", "Fulfillment services", "Strategic planning and project management"], "industries": ["Military", "Commercial & Industrial", "Transportation", "Medical", "Telecommunications"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Flying probe tester (off-site)", "LabView-based functional test systems"], "volume": "Prototype to full production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 2012 -> db", "Headquarters Farmington, New York -> db", "Contract electronics manufacturer of PCB assemblies, cable & wire harnesses, electro-mechanical box builds -> /", "Capabilities: PCB assembly (surface mount, through-hole, multilayer, flexible), cable/wire harness assembly (30-4/0 AWG), box build, testing (flying probe, LabView), conformal coating, machining, cutting, component engineering, fulfillment -> /capabilities", "Industries served: Military, Commercial & Industrial, Transportation, Medical, Telecommunications -> /, /capabilities", "Certifications: SAE AS9100D, ISO 9001:2015, ITAR, UL E157252, CSA LR109165-1, IPC-610, IPC-620, IPC-J-STD, Certified Tyco/AMP subcontractor -> /quality", "Quality standards