UPDATE companies SET description='TSM Corporation operates from Auburn Hills, Michigan, where it was founded in 1978.

The company provides full-service manufacturing of custom components for automotive powertrain, driveline, and chassis applications. Its capabilities span the entire process from design through start of production, supported by over 40 dedicated machining centers, 200-plus production machines, and 24/7 operations. TSM manages every step of development, including in-house re-tooling, design optimization, and program launch.

TSM serves global automotive OEMs and Tier 1 suppliers across more than 40 vehicle platforms. Notable engagements include taking over a failing intake manifold program for a global OEM and delivering it within five weeks, and redesigning a structural support for a major automaker to reduce mass by 25 percent while consolidating two part numbers into one.

The company emphasizes agile production as a core differentiator, describing its responsiveness as part of its DNA. TSM’s quality culture engages all employees and business partners, underpinned by IATF 16949 and ISO 14001 certifications, and aims to deploy customized manufacturing technologies optimized for each product.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 14001','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining (dedicated machining centers)", "Design engineering and design for manufacturability", "Program management and launch support", "Prototyping and low-volume production", "High-volume production", "In-house tooling and re-tooling", "Quality management (IATF 16949)", "Environmental management (ISO 14001)", "Global sourcing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Automotive powertrain", "Automotive driveline", "Automotive chassis"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Rotary dial machine", "Drill presses", "Dedicated machining centers", "Production machines (200+)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Agile production: launches new products on time with exceptional quality under tight milestones", "Full-service capabilities from design through start of production", "24/7 operations with 40+ dedicated machining centers and 200+ machines", "Global partnerships with OEMs and Tier 1 suppliers across 40+ vehicle platforms", "Quality culture engaging all employees and business partners (IATF 16949, ISO 14001)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1978 -> /about-us", "Started with 10 employees, single rotary dial machine and three drill presses -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Auburn Hills, Michigan -> db", "200,000 sq ft production space -> /about-us", "180+ employees -> /about-us", "200+ production machines -> /about-us", "40+ dedicated machining centers -> /about-us", "24/7 operations -> /about-us", "Full-service manufacturer of custom components for automotive powertrain, driveline, chassis -> /", "Capabilities span design through start of production -> /about-us", "Serves OEMs and Tier 1 suppliers across 40+ vehicle platforms -> /about-us", "Intake manifold program takeover delivered in five weeks -> /", "Structural support redesign reduced mass 25% and consolidated two part numbers -> /", "Agile production as core differentiator -> /about-us", "Quality culture engaging all employees and partners -> /about-us", "IATF 16949 certification (expires 2028) -> /about-us", "ISO 14001 certification (expires 2028) -> /about-us", "Environmental policy and sustainability policy -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "TSM is a full-service manufacturer of custom components for automotive powertrain, driveline, and chassis applications.", "founded_year": "1978", "employee_count": "180+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tsm-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='TW Garner Food Company traces its roots to 1929 in Winston-Salem, North Carolina, where the Garner family created a barbecue sauce that gained local popularity during the Great Depression.

Today the company manufactures a line of hot sauces and salsas under the Texas Pete and Green Mountain Gringo labels. Its portfolio includes the original Texas Pete Hot Sauce, two international variants — ¡Sabor! Mexican-Style Hot Sauce and CHA! Sriracha Sauce — and a Non-GMO Verified salsa.

The company serves two primary markets: foodservice operators through its Texas Pete Foodservice division and retail grocery channels through Texas Pete Retail. Green Mountain Gringo products are also distributed through retail outlets.

Garner Foods differentiates itself with clean-label credentials: all products carry Gluten-Free certification, and the Green Mountain Gringo salsa is Non-GMO Verified. The brand also introduced flip-top lids on redesigned bottles for easier dispensing.', certifications=ARRAY['Non-GMO Verified','Gluten-Free']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sauce manufacturing", "Salsa production", "Bottling and packaging"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Retail"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All products certified Gluten-Free", "Green Mountain Gringo salsa Non-GMO Verified", "Flip-top lid packaging on redesigned bottles", "International flavor extensions: Mexican-style and Sriracha hot sauces"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1929 in Winston-Salem, NC -> db", "Family-owned by Garner family -> db", "Produces Texas Pete hot sauce and Green Mountain Gringo salsa -> /", "Non-GMO Verified and Gluten-Free certifications -> /", "Serves foodservice and retail channels -> /", "Offers flip-top lids and international flavor variants -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "TW Garner Food Company began producing a wide variety of sauces", "founded_year": "1929", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tw-garner-food-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tachi-S Engineering U.S.A., Inc. operates from Mt. Juliet, Tennessee, as the U.S. arm of a global automotive seat manufacturer with over 64 years of industry experience. The company focuses on designing, developing, and manufacturing high-quality automotive seats and seat components for original equipment manufacturers.

Its capabilities span the full product lifecycle: design and development, prototyping of trim, foam, and metal parts, and manufacturing including just-in-time frame and complete seat assembly. The company also operates a full range of seat testing services, notably a Servo Sled for collision simulation. Annual output exceeds three million complete seats and four million seat components.

Tachi-S serves automotive OEMs launching cars, trucks, and SUVs worldwide, supporting programs from concept through mass production. Customers rely on the firm for pre-production prototype events, production pad changes during tool modifications, and prototype fixture and frame assembly.

