UPDATE companies SET description='Tasly Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was founded in 2006 and is headquartered in Rockville, Maryland. The company was established to integrate botanical science with modern pharmaceutical innovation, developing safe and effective botanical medicines that complement conventional treatments.

The company’s core focus is the development and manufacture of botanical drugs, most notably T89 (Dantonic®), a herbal medicine-derived compound that has completed an FDA Phase III global clinical trial. Manufacturing takes place on what the company describes as the world’s largest proprietary automatic dripping pill and packaging production line, a fully automated system featuring digital control, high-speed operation, precision pill counting, real-time imprint monitoring, and automated defect removal. The production process follows Good Extracting Practice (GEP) covering extraction, condensation, chromatography, crystallization, filtration, and drying, while quality systems adhere to Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP), Good Agricultural Practice (GAP), and Good Laboratory Practice (GLP). Tasly reports more than 500 worldwide regulatory approvals for its products.

The company has presented Phase III clinical data for T89 at the American College of Cardiology (ACC) 2018, participated in the Trade Winds ASEAN Mission and Business Forum in 2023, and exhibited at BioJapan in 2022, indicating engagement with global pharmaceutical markets and research communities.

Tasly’s stated differentiation rests on bridging traditional healing wisdom with rigorous clinical validation, aiming to revolutionize patient care through scientifically validated botanical medicines. The company emphasizes its first-in-class FDA Phase III achievement for a botanical drug and its fully automated, digitally controlled production line as key factors that set it apart.', certifications=ARRAY['Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP)','Good Agricultural Practice (GAP)','Good Extracting Practice (GEP)','Good Laboratory Practice (GLP)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Botanical drug development", "Automatic dripping pill manufacturing", "Automated packaging", "Extraction", "Condensation", "Chromatography", "Crystallization", "Filtration", "Drying", "Quality control (GMP, GAP, GEP, GLP)", "Clinical trial management (Phase II/III)"], "industries": ["Pharmaceutical", "Botanical medicine", "Healthcare", "Clinical research", "Alternative medicine manufacturing"], "materials": ["Medicinal plants"], "equipment": ["Proprietary automatic dripping pill and packaging production line", "Digital control and analysis system", "High-speed pill counting and labeling equipment", "Real-time automatic online imprint monitoring system", "Automated incompliant product detection and removal system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["World''s largest proprietary automatic dripping pill and packaging production line", "First herbal medicine-derived compound (T89/Dantonic) to complete FDA Phase III global trial", "500+ worldwide regulatory approvals", "Fully automated production with digital control and real-time monitoring", "GMP, GAP, GEP, GLP quality accreditations"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2006 -> /about", "Headquartered in Rockville, Maryland -> /about", "World''s largest proprietary automatic dripping pill and packaging production line -> /quality", "Fully automated production line with digital control, high-speed operation, precision pill counting, label attachment, real-time automatic online imprint monitoring, automated incompliant product detection and removal -> /quality", "Good Extracting Practice (GEP) covering extraction, condensation, chromatography, crystallization, filtration, drying -> /quality", "Good Manufacturing Practice (GMP) accreditation -> /quality", "Good Agricultural Practice (GAP) accreditation -> /quality", "Good Laboratory Practice (GLP) accreditation -> /quality", "T89 (Dantonic) first herbal medicine-derived compound to complete FDA Phase III global trial -> /about", "500+ worldwide regulatory approvals -> /about", "Presented Phase III clinical data for T89 at ACC 2018 -> /about", "Participated in Trade Winds ASEAN Mission and Business Forum 2023 -> /about", "Exhibited at BioJapan 2022 -> /about", "Mission to integrate botanical science with modern pharmaceutical innovation -> /about", "Commitment to bridging traditional healing wisdom with clinical validation -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Tasly Group has the world''s largest proprietary automatic dripping pill and packaging production line.", "founded_year": "2006", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tasly-pharmaceuticals-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tech Energy America LLC is a wholesale electrical distributor based in Scottsdale, Arizona, founded in 2009. The company was started to address contractors'' and industrial buyers'' difficulties in obtaining straightforward pricing and reliable delivery from large distributors.

The company operates a Scottsdale warehouse and an in-house switchgear assembly line, distributing products from manufacturers such as JST Power, CME Wire, Priority Wire, Southwire, and Square D/Schneider Electric. It also manufactures UL-listed switchgear, panelboards, and VFDs, and supplies PV wire, XHHW-2 wire, EV charging equipment, and related materials.

Its customers include licensed electrical contractors, solar EPCs (such as Solar Gain Inc.), industrial buyers, and resellers across Arizona and nationwide. The company serves the solar, EV charging, commercial, and residential construction sectors.

The company emphasizes bilingual (English/Spanish) service across all functions, same-day RFQ turnaround for most BOMs, and documentation by default with spec sheets and warranty paperwork. It was founded to provide straight pricing and reliable delivery, and it combines distribution with in-house manufacturing to offer a single source for projects.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale electrical distribution", "In-house UL-listed switchgear manufacturing", "Panelboard assembly", "VFD assembly", "Bilingual account management and sales (EN/ES)", "Same-day RFQ and quoting", "Project material kitting", "Nationwide freight shipping", "Solar PV wire and XHHW-2 wire supply", "EV charging equipment supply", "Square D/Schneider Electric authorized distribution", "JST Power, CME Wire, Priority Wire, Southwire authorized representation"], "industries": ["Electrical contracting", "Industrial", "Solar energy", "EV charging infrastructure", "Commercial construction", "Residential construction"], "materials": ["PV wire", "XHHW-2 wire", "Copper conductors", "Aluminum conductors", "Steel conduit", "PVC conduit", "Transformers", "Switchgear components", "Panelboards", "Breakers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "4\u20138 weeks for standard 480V/600V switchgear assemblies; 24\u201348 business hours for RFQ-to-quote; same-day for stock items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Bilingual English/Spanish service from ownership through order logistics", "Same-day RFQ turnaround on most BOMs", "Documentation by default with spec sheets and manufacturer warranty paperwork", "In-house UL-listed switchgear manufacturing with 4\u20138 week lead times", "Single-source quoting for both manufactured switchgear and distributed materials"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 in Scottsdale, AZ -> /about", "Wholesale electrical distributor of transformers, wire & cable, UL-listed switchgear -> /", "In-house UL-listed switchgear manufacturing -> /", 