UPDATE companies SET description='TechNH, Inc. was founded in 1982 in a small corner of a Nashua, New Hampshire mill building. Now headquartered in Merrimack, NH, the company has grown from a modest operation into a global precision injection molder.

The company specializes in custom plastic injection molding, offering insert molding, over-molding, and in-house mold making and repair. Its facility houses presses ranging from 16 to 780 tons, capable of shot weights from 1/2 ounce to 128 ounces. Services extend to design for manufacturability, mold flow analysis, cleanroom molding, and secondary operations such as pad printing, assembly, and packaging. An in-house regulatory team supports compliance with ISO 13485:2016, ITAR, FDA 21 CFR 820, and UL standards, including IQ/OQ/PQ validation.

TechNH serves medical device, defense, alternative energy, water treatment, and industrial customers. Testimonials reference clients in Massachusetts, Pennsylvania, and New Hampshire, including healthcare and industrial OEMs. The company assigns each project a dedicated team comprising an account manager, customer service representative, program manager, and a degreed plastics engineer.

TechNH emphasizes a 5-step tool transfer process designed to protect supply continuity and confirm tool condition without production downtime. Core values—adaptability, integrity, enthusiasm, pride in work, and reliability—guide operations. Nearly 40% of the workforce has more than five years'' tenure, and about a quarter have exceeded a decade, reflecting a culture the company cites as a differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ITAR','FDA 21 CFR 820','UL Recognized']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Insert molding", "Over-molding", "Mold making", "Mold repair", "Design for manufacturability", "Mold flow analysis", "Cleanroom molding", "Pad printing", "Assembly", "Packaging", "Tool transfer", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation", "Regulatory compliance (ISO 13485, ITAR, FDA, UL)"], "industries": ["Medical", "Defense", "Alternative Energy", "Water Treatment", "Industrial Applications"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["5-step tool transfer process protects supply continuity and confirms tool condition", "In-house regulatory team for ISO 13485, ITAR, FDA, and UL compliance", "In-house mold-making and repair capabilities", "Dedicated project team including a degreed plastics engineer", "Presses from 16 to 780 tons with shot weights up to 128 ounces"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1982 in Nashua, NH -> /about", "Headquartered in Merrimack, NH -> db", "ISO 13485:2016 certified -> /capabilities", "ITAR registered -> /capabilities", "Machines 16-780 tons -> /capabilities", "Shot weight 1/2 to 128 ounces -> /capabilities", "Insert molding and over-molding -> /capabilities", "In-house mold making and repair -> /capabilities", "Design for manufacturability and mold flow analysis -> /capabilities", "Cleanroom molding -> /capabilities", "Secondary services: pad printing, assembly, packaging -> /capabilities", "5-step tool transfer process -> /", "Industries: Medical, Defense, Alterna