UPDATE companies SET description='Tegra Medical LLC operates as a contract manufacturer of medical devices from its headquarters in Franklin, Massachusetts. The company maintains a global footprint with production facilities in the United States, Costa Rica, Switzerland, Malaysia, China, and Singapore, including sites in Hernando, Dartmouth, Altstätten, Hallau, Heerbrugg, Johor Bahru, and Nantong City. This distributed network supports a local-for-local strategy aimed at reducing supply-chain risk and shipping costs for OEM customers.

The firm provides end-to-end manufacturing services spanning design and prototyping through its GENESIS Tech Center® to full-scale production, assembly, packaging, and sterilization. Core processes include injection molding, precision wire and tubing fabrication with secondary operations such as grinding, cutting, coating, end treatments, and custom mandrel production. A Quick Wire & Tubing store stocks stainless steel, nitinol, and coated wire plus tubing for rapid prototyping needs.

Tegra serves medical device OEMs across specialties including oncology, ophthalmics, women''s health, advanced orthopedics, minimally invasive surgery, drug delivery, cardiovascular and neurology, cardiac rhythm management, and robotic-assisted surgery. The company emphasizes collaboration with OEM partners to deliver precision-engineered instruments, implants, and finished devices.

Differentiators cited by the company include its integrated end-to-end model, the GENESIS Tech Center for accelerated development, a quality system built on ISO 13485 certification and FDA QSR compliance with black-belt engineers and real-time SPC, and sustainability investments such as solar installations and Industry 4.0 digitalization.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','FDA QSR compliance','FDA registered medical device manufacturer']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Molding", "Prototyping & Product Development (GENESIS Tech Center)", "Assembly, Packaging, & Sterilization", "Wire & Tubing Grinding", "Wire & Tubing Cutting", "Wire & Tubing Coating", "Wire & Tubing End Treatments", "Custom Mandrel Production", "Full-Scale Production", "Design Services", "Statistical Process Control (SPC)", "Lean Manufacturing / Six Sigma", "Validated Processes", "IQ/OQ/PQ Procedures", "PFMEA", "Design of Experiments (DOE)", "Control Plans"], "industries": ["Oncology", "Ophthalmic", "Women''s Health", "Advanced Orthopedics", "Minimally Invasive Surgery", "Drug Delivery", "Cardiovascular and Neurology", "Cardiac Rhythm Management", "Robotic Assisted Surgery"], "materials": ["Stainless Steel Wire", "Nitinol Wire", "Coated Wire", "Tubing"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["True end-to-end contract manufacturing from design to sterilization", "GENESIS Tech Center\u00ae for prototyping and product development", "Local-for-local manufacturing across six countries", "ISO 13485 certified and FDA QSR compliant with black-belt engineers", "Quick Wire & Tubing store with ready-to-ship inventory"], "facts_used": ["Contract manufacturer of medical devices -> db description, home page", "Headquarters in Franklin, Massachusetts -> db hq_city, hq_state_label", "Global facilities in US, Costa Rica, Switzerland, Malaysia, China, Singapore -> home page", "Specific site locations: Hernando, Dartmouth, Altst\u00e4tten, Hallau, Heerbrugg, Joho