UPDATE companies SET description='Telink Semiconductor is headquartered in Tustin, California, and was founded in 2014. No founder names or ownership structure are disclosed in the available sources.

The company develops SoCs that integrate Bluetooth Low Energy, Bluetooth Classic, Bluetooth Mesh, Zigbee, Thread, Matter, Wi-Fi 6, Amazon Sidewalk, and 2.4 GHz proprietary protocols. Product families include the TL323X series for Matter and Amazon Sidewalk, the automotive-grade TL3225 series, the high-performance TL721X series, and the TL3228 targeting 8 KHz wireless gaming peripherals. Telink supports development with software development kits (SDKs), an integrated development environment, hardware design guidelines, reference designs, a product selection tool, and a technical forum staffed by its engineers.

Telink’s solutions are used in smart home devices such as lighting and door locks, wireless audio and gaming accessories requiring low latency, human input devices including keyboards and mice, universal remote controls for major smart TV and set-top box brands, industrial IoT nodes, and electronic shelf labels for smart retail. The company cites deployments with some of the world’s largest smart TV, set-top box, and OTT box manufacturers.

Telink emphasizes ultra-low power efficiency, multi-protocol coexistence on a single chip, and certification to Thread, OpenThread, and Matter standards as key differentiators. It positions its one-stop development ecosystem — silicon, software, tools, and direct engineering support — as a way to accelerate customers’ time-to-market.', certifications=ARRAY['ROHS','Thread certified','OpenThread certified','Matter certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fabless semiconductor design", "Multi-protocol wireless SoC development", "SDK and firmware development", "Reference design provision", "Technical support forum", "Product selection tool", "AI-assisted product support"], "industries": ["Smart home", "Wireless audio", "Wireless gaming", "Industrial IoT", "Automotive", "Smart retail", "Human input devices (HID)", "Remote controls", "Electronic shelf labels (ESL)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Multi-protocol wireless SoCs supporting Bluetooth, Zigbee, Thread, Matter, Wi-Fi, and proprietary 2.4 GHz", "Ultra-low power efficiency for battery-operated IoT devices", "Thread, OpenThread, and Matter certified solutions", "Comprehensive SDKs, IDE, reference designs, and technical forum support", "Automotive-grade qualified product line (TL3225 series)"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters Tustin, California -> db", "Founded 2014 -> db", "Certification ROHS -> db", "Product families TL323X, TL3225, TL721X, TL3228 -> page /", "Protocols: Bluetooth LE, Classic, Mesh, Zigbee, Thread, Matter, Wi-Fi 6, Amazon Sidewalk, 2.4 GHz proprietary -> page /", "Applications: smart home, wireless audio, wireless gaming, industrial, automotive, smart retail, HID, remote controls, ESL -> page /", "Development ecosystem: SDKs, IDE, reference designs, product selector, technical forum -> page /", "Thread, OpenThread, Matter certified -> page /", "Automotive-grade TL3225 series -> page /", "Global sales/support offices listed -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Telink | Chips for a Smarter IoT ... Telink SoCs are now certified by Thread and OpenThread.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='telink-semiconductor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Terrain Biomedical, Inc. is based in Buffalo Grove, Illinois. The company was established in 2005 to provide a cost-effective, full-life-cycle approach to medical equipment transactions. Founded by biomedical engineers who believed clients deserved more than generic sales, the firm began as a refurbisher and seller of sterilizers and has since expanded into a comprehensive resource for equipment acquisition, service, and support.

The company refurbishes, sells, rents, and services a wide range of medical devices, including autoclaves, defibrillators, fetal monitors, patient monitors, electrosurgical units, and surgical tables. Its degreed biomedical engineers follow strict processes to restore used equipment to manufacturer-recommended specifications, performing repairs, preventative maintenance, electrical safety inspections, and operational testing. Terrain also installs equipment, trains staff, consults on equipment planning, and manages equipment removal. The facility handles brands such as Zoll, Corometrics, Mindray, and STERIS, though facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

The firm differentiates itself by emphasizing three pillars: ensuring equipment works, ensuring it is necessary, and ensuring it lasts. Its engineers are qualified to perform repairs and recertifications on behalf of several major manufacturers, and the company offers free white-glove local delivery, a rental fleet for immediate deployment, and a commitment to complete equipment life-cycle management rather than one-time sales.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical equipment refurbishment", "Medical equipment sales", "Medical equipment rental", "Preventative maintenance", "Equipment repair", "Installation and training", "Consultation services", "Equipment removal", "Electrical safety inspection", "Operational testing", "Performance checks", "Field service", "Buying used equipment"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Skilled nursing facilities", "Rehabilitation facilities", "Hospitals", "Clinics"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Autoclaves", "Bladder scanners", "Defibrillators (Zoll R Series)", "ECG-EKG machines", "Electrosurgical units", "Endoscopy systems", "Exam chairs", "Fetal monitors (Corometrics 170)", "Patient monitors (Mindray Passport 12m)", "Pulse oximeters", "Surgical tables (STERIS Amsco 3080)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Degreed biomedical engineers perform repairs and recertifications to manufacturer specifications", "Free white-glove local delivery on equipment orders", "Full equipment life-cycle services from purchase through maintenance and removal", "Rental programs for emergency, short-term, and long-term needs", "Buys used medical equipment offering competitive prices"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2005 -> db (description)", "Headquarters in Buffalo Grove, Illinois -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label)", "Refurbishes and sells sterilizers and medical equipment -> db (description)", "Provides biomedical engineering services, repair, maintenance, installation, training, consultation, rental