UPDATE companies SET description='Teton Valley Brands operates from Caldwell, Idaho, where it produces snack foods using locally sourced ingredients. The company was established to create potato chips made exclusively from Idaho potatoes, though a founding year is not publicly disclosed. Ownership details are not specified, but the business emphasizes its Idaho roots and community-based workforce.

The company manufactures two primary product lines: Real Idaho® Potato Chips and Tallow & Stone tortilla chips. Potato chips are made from hand-selected Idaho potatoes supplied by Cranney Farms, a multi-generational farm in Oakley, Idaho. The tortilla chips are cooked in traditional beef tallow rather than seed oils. Production takes place in a state-of-the-art facility in Caldwell that currently employs ten people, handling the entire process from manufacturing through shipping.

Teton Valley Brands serves retail channels across Idaho''s Treasure Valley, with products stocked in stores carrying collegiate-branded chips produced in partnership with Boise State Athletics and the University of Idaho Athletics. The company also works directly with its potato supplier, Cranney Farms, as a strategic partner.

The brand differentiates itself through a simple-ingredient philosophy: all products are gluten-free, non-GMO, and free of artificial colors, flavors, preservatives, hydrogenated oils, and refined salts. The company states that keeping the full production cycle in Idaho—from potato farming to finished packaging—ensures quality and supports the local economy.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Potato chip manufacturing", "Tortilla chip manufacturing", "Tallow-based frying", "Seasoning and packaging", "Private label / collegiate branding"], "industries": ["Snack food manufacturing", "Retail food distribution", "Collegiate licensing"], "materials": ["Idaho potatoes", "Beef tallow", "Corn (for tortilla chips)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Made with 100% Real Idaho\u00ae potatoes from Idaho farms", "All-natural, gluten-free, non-GMO, no artificial preservatives", "Tortilla chips cooked in traditional beef tallow", "Entire manufacturing process kept in Idaho", "Collegiate co-branded chips with Boise State and University of Idaho"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Caldwell, Idaho -> /", "Manufactures Real Idaho\u00ae Potato Chips and Tallow & Stone tortilla chips -> /", "Uses 100% Real Idaho potatoes sourced from Cranney Farms in Oakley, Idaho -> /", "Facility employs ten people -> /", "Partnerships with Boise State Athletics and University of Idaho Athletics for branded chips -> /", "Products are gluten-free, non-GMO, no artificial preservatives -> /", "Tortilla chips cooked in traditional tallow -> /", "State-of-the-art manufacturing facility in Caldwell -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our state of the art manufacturing facility is located just west of Boise, in Caldwell, ID.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "10", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::js