UPDATE companies SET description='Texas Instruments traces its roots to 1930 when Geophysical Service Inc., an oil and gas exploration venture, opened in Dallas, Texas. The founders’ entrepreneurial drive led the company into electronics during World War II, and by 1951 it was renamed Texas Instruments Incorporated.

TI designs, fabricates, packages, and tests analog and embedded processing chips, offering a portfolio of more than 80,000 products. Its global manufacturing network includes 300 mm wafer fabs that run on 100 % renewable electricity, and the company reports producing tens of billions of chips each year. With roughly 33,000 employees and over 100,000 customers, TI handles everything from process technology and design through final test and delivery.

The company’s components serve automotive, industrial, consumer electronics, communications, data center, personal electronics, and medical equipment markets. Engineers at automakers, industrial automation firms, smartphone makers, and data‑center operators rely on TI’s analog ICs, microcontrollers, and wireless transceivers for applications ranging from vehicle electrification to AI‑driven servers.

TI says its founding purpose was to make electronics more affordable through semiconductors, a mission that still guides its three core ambitions: act like long‑term owners, adapt to a changing world, and build a company its people are proud of. The firm emphasizes supply‑chain resilience, noting that its manufacturing expertise lets customers get products when they need them, regardless of geopolitical conditions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Analog IC design", "Embedded processor design", "Wafer fabrication (300mm)", "Semiconductor packaging", "Semiconductor test", "Quality and reliability testing", "Anti-counterfeit programs", "Product change notification", "Product life cycle management", "Environmental compliance (RoHS, lead-free)", "Automotive PPAP support", "Failure analysis", "Material content search", "Moisture sensitivity level classification", "Part marking lookup"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Industrial", "Consumer Electronics", "Communication", "Data Center", "Personal Electronics", "Medical Equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["300mm wafer fabs", "Kilby Labs", "DLP\u00ae chip technology"], "volume": "Tens of billions of chips per year", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Broad portfolio of 80,000+ analog and embedded products", "Global 300\u202fmm wafer fabs powered by 100\u202f% renewable electricity", "Decades of manufacturing expertise ensuring supply\u2011chain resilience", "40,000+ patents held worldwide", "Annual R&D investment exceeding $2\u202fB"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1930 as Geophysical Service Inc. -> /about", "Headquartered in Dallas, Texas -> /about", "33,000+ employees -> /about", "80,000+ products -> /about", "Tens of billions of chips produced yearly -> /about", "100% renewable electricity at 300mm wafer fabs -> /", "40,000+ patents worldwide -> /", "$2B+ annual R&D investment -> /", "Industries served: automotive, industrial, consumer electronics, communication -> db, /abou