UPDATE companies SET description='The Plastics Group of America (TPG) is headquartered in Woonsocket, Rhode Island, where it was founded in 1973 by Bob Lebeaux as Ralco Industries, a one-man scrap trading operation. The business adopted its current name in 1988 after merging Ralco, the Polifil® compounding line, and the Transcontinental Polymers recycling unit.

TPG operates over 300,000 square feet of manufacturing space in Woonsocket and runs a 24/7 production schedule. Its core business is custom compounding of Polifil® polypropylene-based reinforced resins, using mineral, talc, calcium, glass, and barium additives to meet specific physical, mechanical, and thermal requirements. An on-site quality control laboratory equipped with melt index, Izod, flexural, tensile, DSC, moisture, ash, Gardner impact, and color testing instruments certifies every batch, whether the order is 100 pounds or one million pounds. The company also provides recycling and toll processing services, densifying, guillotining, and extruding scrap into reusable material, and acts as a resin broker and distributor with stocking points across the continental United States.

The compounded resins serve processors in appliance, automotive, construction, consumer housewares and disposables, furniture, industrial/institutional/electronic, medical and personal care, packaging, and pump/pool/spa/irrigation markets. TPG''s ISO 9001-certified facility supplies molders, extruders, and blow-molding operations that require consistent, specification-grade thermoplastics.

TPG emphasizes its asset-based manufacturing model combined with a full-service approach: free commercial color matching, technical consulting through its TPGOA Technical Insights library, and a commitment to on-time, on-budget delivery. The company traces its differentiation to the 1980 launch of custom compounding under the Polifil® brand and its early adoption of ISO 9002 certification in 1996, followed by an OSHA SHARP award in 1997.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','OSHA SHARP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom compounding of polypropylene-based reinforced resins", "Recycling and toll processing (densifying, guillotining, extruding)", "Resin distribution and brokerage", "Color matching (commercial, no-charge)", "Quality control testing (Melt Index, Izod, Flexural, Tensile, DSC, Moisture Content, Ash Content, Gardner Impact, Color Testing)", "Technical consulting (TPGOA Technical Insights)", "Rotational molding", "Extrusion coating and lamination", "Gas injection molding", "Spiral flow molding", "Insert molding", "Hot plate welding"], "industries": ["Appliance", "Automotive", "Construction", "Consumer Housewares and Disposables", "Furniture", "Industrial/Institutional/Electronic", "Medical & Personal Care", "Packaging", "Pump/Pool/Spa/Irrigation"], "materials": ["Polypropylene", "Glass-filled polypropylene", "Mineral-filled polypropylene", "Talc-filled polypropylene", "Calcium-filled polypropylene", "Barium-filled polypropylene", "Recycled thermoplastics"], "equipment": ["Extruders", "Grinders", "Balers", "On-line rheometers", "Testing laboratory equipment (Melt Index, Izod, Flexural, Tensile, DSC, Moisture, Ash, Gardner Impact, Color testing)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Asset-based manufacturer with 300,000+ sq ft facility and 24/7 production", "On-site ISO 9001-certified testing laboratory for every batch", "Free commercial color-matching service with lot-to-lot consistency", "Recycling and toll processing of scrap plastics into usable resin", "Distribution network across the continental United States"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Woonsocket, RI -> /about-us", "Founded 1973 by Bob Lebeaux as Ralco Industries -> /about-us", "Family-owned with Marti Lebeaux (President/CEO), Heidi Lebeaux (HR), Jacob Lebeaux (Maintenance Director) -> /about-us", "Name changed to The Plastics Group of America in 1988 -> /about-us", "Over 300,000 sq ft manufacturing space -> /", "24/7 production schedule -> /about-us", "Custom compounding of Polifil\u00ae polypropylene-based reinforced resins -> /", "Additives: mineral, talc, calcium, glass, barium -> /about-us", "On-site quality control lab with listed test capabilities -> /services", "Order range 100 lbs to 1 million lbs -> /", "Recycling/toll processing: densifying, guillotining, extruding -> /services", "Resin broker and distributor with stocking points across continental US -> /services", "ISO 9001 certified -> /about-us, db", "OSHA SHARP award 1997 -> /about-us", "Industries served list -> /about-us", "60+ employees, $50M+ annual revenue -> /about-us", "Free commercial color matching -> /services", "Technical consulting via TPGOA Technical Insights -> /services", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "While also a broker and distributor, we are primarily an asset-based manufacturer, capable of custom-compounding resins to the physical, mechanical, and thermal specifications your application requires.", "founded_year": "1973", "employee_count": "60+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/6985369/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-plastics-group-of-america' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Sheet Metal Shop operates from Columbus, Ohio, where it has built a reputation for precision sheet metal fabrication. The business is veteran-owned and family-owned, though its founding year is not publicly disclosed.

The shop provides a wide range of fabrication services, including plasma cutting, aluminum and stainless steel welding, custom ductwork, grease ducts, roof curbs, roof rails, structural framing, anti-theft security cages, fire wrap installation, and artistic metalwork. It works with stainless steel, aluminum, carbon steel, and black iron, serving both residential and commercial projects. No facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures are published.

Its customer base spans construction, manufacturing, and HVAC sectors, with commercial and industrial clients throughout Central Ohio. The company also serves residential customers for custom metal artistry, HVAC components, and planters.

The company highlights its R-Stamp certification as evidence of adherence to industry standards, and emphasizes its veteran and family-owned legacy combined with state-of-the-art technology as key differentiators. It states that its commitment to quality, precision, and customer satisfaction sets it apart from other fabricators.', certifications=ARRAY['R-Stamp']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Aluminum repair", "Aluminum welding", "Angle iron fabrication", "Anti-theft security cage fabrication", "Canvas connector fabrication", "Carbon steel fabrication", "Curb adapter fabrication", "Custom fabrication", "Custom HVAC sheet metal fabrication", "Duct fabrication", "Stainless steel and aluminum fabrication", "Fire wrap installation", "Grease duct fabrication", "Roof curb fabrication", "Roof rail fabrication", "Plasma cutting", "Stainless steel welding", "Structural and framing fabrication", "Artistic welding", "Industrial welding", "Architectural welding"], "industries": ["Construction", "Manufacturing", "HVAC (residential and commercial)"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Carbon steel", "Black iron"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["R-Stamp certified for precision fabrication", "Veteran-owned and family-owned legacy", "State-of-the-art technology including plasma cutting and welding", "Custom fabrication tailored to each project''s requirements", "Serves commercial, industrial, and residential clients"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Columbus, Ohio -> /", "Veteran and family-owned legacy -> /about-us", "R-Stamp certified -> /", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, carbon steel, black iron -> /about-us", "Industries served: construction, manufacturing, HVAC (residential and commercial) -> /about-us", "Capabilities: plasma cutting, welding, duct fabrication, custom fabrication, structural framing, artistic welding -> /services", "Differentiators: veteran and family-owned legacy, state-of-the-art techn