UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Arab, Alabama, The Wooden Nickel builds custom live edge furniture from locally sourced hardwood slabs. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed; it operates as a shop where each piece begins with a slab selected for its natural character.

The shop produces dining tables, desks, adjustable workstations, and contract-grade furniture for commercial spaces. The process is deliberately slow: logs from tree services and loggers are kiln-dried and stabilized, then flattened, sanded, and inspected for cracks or knots that may receive resin filling. Finishes are applied in multiple hand-rubbed coats, and steel bases—fabricated from high-tolerance steel—are fitted to ensure level, wobble-free assembly. The company notes that most production is custom, ranging from single items to larger commercial orders.

Customers include residential clients such as a Marshall County family that commissioned a three-generation dining table, as well as local businesses needing tables and work surfaces for offices, break rooms, and public areas. The firm has supplied several area companies with thicker slabs, reinforced bases, and durable finishes designed for daily wear.

The Wooden Nickel emphasizes careful material selection, honest construction, and an unhurried timeline. As the owners describe it, the goal is furniture that ''doesn''t draw attention to itself'' but ''just keeps working year after year''—built to be used, built to last, and built for real life.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Live edge slab selection", "Kiln drying and stabilization", "Slab flattening and sanding", "Resin crack and knot filling", "Multi-coat hand-rubbed finishing", "Steel base fabrication", "Adjustable desk frame assembly", "Custom furniture design", "Contract furniture manufacturing"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Commercial office furniture", "Contract furniture"], "materials": ["Kiln-dried hardwood", "Steel", "Epoxy resin"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Slow, deliberate process with kiln-dried and stabilized slabs", "Steel bases fabricated in-house from high-tolerance steel", "Logs sourced from local tree services and loggers", "No templates or shortcuts; each slab unique", "Contract-grade durability for commercial use"], "facts_used": ["Location: Arab, Alabama -> db", "Custom live edge furniture production -> page \"/\"", "Process: kiln drying, stabilization, flattening, sanding, resin filling, hand-rubbed finishing -> page \"/\"", "Steel bases fabricated from high-tolerance steel -> page \"/\"", "Logs sourced from tree services and loggers -> capabilities array (first element)", "Residential and commercial customers (Marshall County family, local businesses) -> page \"/\"", "Contract furniture for offices, break rooms, public spaces -> page \"/\"", "Emphasis on slow, careful process and durability -> page \"/\"", "Adjustable desk frames offered -> page \"/\""], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We walked through slab options together, talked about grain patterns, and settled on a wide piece of kiln-dried hardwood with just enough natural curve to keep its character. The base was simple steel, finished dark so the wood stayed the star of the show.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-wooden-nickel-custom-live-edge-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Thos. Moser’s Freeport showroom occupies a restored nineteenth-century home in Freeport, Maine, two blocks north of L.L.Bean’s flagship store.

The showroom spans two full floors displaying classic and current Thos. Moser furniture designs alongside Maine artwork. An attached carriage house functions as an outlet annex where unique pieces are available for immediate purchase. The location operates Monday through Saturday 10 a.m.–5 p.m. and Sunday noon–5 p.m., and offers scheduled consultations for standard and custom furniture designs through its Customer in Residence (CIR) program, managed by Steve Wyman.

The product lineup includes commercial products, and the CIR program caters to clients exploring custom designs. The space also hosts art exhibitions, such as the “Dedicated to Art” display running through October 31, 2026, pairing paintings and prints with furniture.

