UPDATE companies SET description='Throttle Down Kustoms operates from Moore, Montana, where it was established in April 2004 after founder Jeremy Pulse purchased his former employer, Advance Frame Works. Pulse had begun building custom truck bumpers in his spare time during the early 2000s, and growing demand led him to transition to full-time fabrication.

The company designs, engineers, and builds steel front and rear bumpers for Chevrolet Silverado, Dodge Ram, Ford F-Series, and GMC Sierra trucks, as well as steel Jeep frames and skid plates. Production relies on CNC laser-cut PNO steel plate (3/16″ and 1/4″) and CNC mandrel-bent frames using 2″×4″ A500 rectangular tubing, all hand-welded by certified fabricators. A separate line, TreeDogKustoms, produces lightweight aluminum dog boxes for trucks, ATVs, and UTVs. The shop runs a dedicated team of certified fabricators, each trained in chassis fabrication programs.

Customers range from ranch hands and oil-field workers needing heavy-duty bumper upgrades to off-road enthusiasts seeking grille guards, integrated LED lighting, and rock-crawling frames. The company also fulfills custom fabrication requests such as enclosed trailers, street rods, and diesel-powered truggies. Products ship worldwide with a typical lead time of 8 to 12 weeks.

Throttle Down Kustoms emphasizes U.S. manufacturing, a lifetime warranty on every product, and mandrel-bent frames that avoid welded joints for greater strength and precision. Pulse’s WyoTech degree in Auto Body Technology and Chassis Fabrication underpins the engineering approach, and the company hires only graduates of reputable fabrication programs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC laser cutting", "Hand welding", "CNC mandrel bending", "Frame fabrication", "Bumper fabrication", "Skid plate fabrication", "Aluminum dog box fabrication", "Custom metal fabrication", "Chassis fabrication", "Auto body technology"], "industries": ["Light truck aftermarket", "Off-road vehicle accessories", "Powersports accessories (ATV/UTV)", "Custom metal fabrication"], "materials": ["PNO steel plate", "A500 structural tubing", "Aluminum", "Grade 8 steel hardware"], "equipment": ["CNC laser cutter", "CNC mandrel bender"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "8 to 12 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime warranty on all products", "Mandrel-bent frames (no welded frames)", "CNC laser-cut PNO steel plate, hand-welded by certified fabricators", "Made in USA (Moore, Montana)", "Custom fabrication beyond bumpers (trailers, buggies, dog boxes)"], "facts_used": ["Founded April 2004 after Jeremy Pulse bought Advance Frame Works -> /about", "Located in Moore, Montana -> db, /about", "Owner/founder Jeremy Pulse with WyoTech degree in Auto Body Technology and Chassis Fabrication -> /about", "Products: steel bumpers for Chevy Silverado, Dodge RAM, Ford F-Series, GMC Sierra; steel Jeep frames and skid plates; aluminum dog boxes -> /, /about", "Processes: CNC laser cut PNO steel plate, hand welded by certified professionals, CNC mandrel bent frames using A500 tubing -> /, /about", "Lifetime warranty on all products -> /, /about", "Custom fabrications: enclosed trailers, Jeep frames, rock crawling buggies, street rods, diesel powered truggies -> /about", "Lead time 8-12 weeks -> /", "Made in USA -> /, /about", "Team of certified fabricators graduated from reputable chassis fabrication programs -> /about", "Materials: PNO steel plate, A500 tubing, aluminum, Grade 8 hardware -> /, /about", "Equipment: CNC laser cutter, CNC mandrel bender -> /, /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We design, engineer, and construct rugged steel front bumpers and rear bumpers for Chevy Silverado, Dodge RAM, Ford F-Series, and GMC Sierra trucks.", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='throttle-down-kustoms-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Thunderbird Molding operates from Elkhart, Indiana, with additional facilities in Shelbyville, Illinois, and Greensboro. The company is Thunderbird-owned and actively managed, though its founding year and founders are not publicly disclosed. It began as a resource for high-precision custom plastic injection molding and contract manufacturing.

The company provides comprehensive mold design, prototyping, engineering, production, and assembly services. Its capabilities include custom plastic injection molding, insert molding, over molding via press-to-press transfer, finishing, and secondary operations. With presses ranging up to 1,500 tons and an inventory of more than 800 molds, Thunderbird supports scalable production of parts in the millions as well as economical short-run projects using quick-mold-change systems and proprietary batch molding procedures. It also offers 3D printing for low-volume production using carbon printing technology.

Thunderbird serves medical device manufacturers, defense contractors, automotive OEMs, and producers of drinkware and lighting. The company has helped a medical device manufacturer achieve regulatory compliance and an automaker find solutions with advanced molding processes. Its lens-grade parts, made from contaminant-free polymers, meet critical defense industry specifications.

Thunderbird differentiates itself through repeatable part tolerances of ±0.0002 inches, automated 3D video inspection, and a quality system registered to ISO 9001:2015, ITAR, PPAP, SPI, and UL QMMY2. The company cites a 99% success rate when reworking close-tolerance molds to compensate for shrinkage and warpage, and a 2.5-second cycle time on an 8-cavity mold.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR registered','PPAP compliant','SPI compliant','UL QMMY2 certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Insert molding", "Over molding (press-to-press transfer)", "Finishing and secondary services", "Mold design", "Prototyping", "Engineering support", "Production molding", "Assembly", "Injection molding tool transfer", "3D printing (carbon printing)", "Short-run/low-volume production", "Prototype-to-production support"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Defense", "Automotive", "Drinkware", "Lighting"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Presses up to 1,500 tons", "Quick-mold-change system", "3D printing (carbon printing)", "Automated 3D video inspection", "Multi-sensor metrology systems", "High-end moisture analyzers", "Digital height gauges", "Gauge pins", "Torque scales", "Micrometers", "Spectrophotometer"], "volume": "Scalable production of parts in the millions; economical short-run projects", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.0002 in", "built_on": ["Repeatable part tolerances to \u00b10.0002 inches", "ISO 9001:2015 registered quality system", "ITAR registered for defense work", "99% success rate reworking close-tolerance molds", "2.5-second cycle time on 8-cavity mold"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Elkhart, Indiana -> db", "Additional locations: Shelbyville, Illinois; Greensboro -> / (home page)", "Ownership: Thunderbird-owned and actively managed -> /quality", "Processes: custom plastic injection molding, insert molding, over molding, finishing, mold design, prototyping, engineering, production, assembly, tool transf